content:
Find a database namespace within a multi-database source, when you don&rsquo;t know its exact name.
API listDatabases(...) always accepts an optional query/maxResults; omit them to simply list every database.
//JAVA 25+ //DEPS com.github.nbbrd.sdmx-dl:sdmx-dl-standalone:3.2.0 import sdmxdl.*; import sdmxdl.web.SdmxWebManager; void main() throws Exception { Provider ecb = SdmxWebManager.ofServiceLoader().usingName(&#34;ECB&#34;); // List every database ecb.listDatabases(DatabasesRequest.DEFAULT) .forEach(database -&gt; IO.println(database.getRef())); // Search by name ecb.listDatabases(DatabasesRequest.builder() .query(&#34;central&#34;) .maxResults(5) .build()) .forEach(database -&gt; IO.println(database.getRef())); } CLI sdmx-dl list databases ECB sdmx-dl list databases ECB -q &#34;central&#34; -m 5 WS REST curl &#34;localhost:4559/sdmx-dl/v2/ECB/databases&#34; curl -G localhost:4559/sdmx-dl/v2/ECB/databases \ --data-urlencode &#34;query=central&#34; \ --data-urlencode &#34;maxResults=5&#34; gRPC grpcurl -d &#39;{&#34;source&#34;:&#34;ECB&#34;}&#39; -plaintext localhost:4557 sdmxdl.grpc.v2.SdmxWebManager.ListDatabases grpcurl -d &#39;{&#34;source&#34;:&#34;ECB&#34;,&#34;query&#34;:&#34;central&#34;,&#34;maxResults&#34;:5}&#39; -plaintext localhost:4557 sdmxdl.grpc.v2.SdmxWebManager.ListDatabases Notes Discovery and search are the same call: pass a query/maxResults to search within a source, or omit them to list every database it exposes. Most sources expose a single default database, so this feature is only useful for multi-database providers. Search is scoped to one source at a time; use Discover sources first if you don&rsquo;t know which source to search within. Related features Discover sources Discover flows

